Arara Code: log expected builtin/user extension deduplication at debug level.

Why a patch: extension scanning runs before activation and extension APIs cannot
change its diagnostic level. The existing selection and version comparison are
unchanged; the redundant same-or-older user installation stays on disk.
Touches: extensionsUtil.ts.

--- a/src/vs/workbench/services/extensions/common/extensionsUtil.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/services/extensions/common/extensionsUtil.ts
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 		if (extension) {
 			if (extension.isBuiltin) {
 				if (semver.gte(extension.version, userExtension.version)) {
-					logService.warn(`Skipping extension ${userExtension.extensionLocation.path} in favour of the builtin extension ${extension.extensionLocation.path}.`);
+					logService.debug(`Skipping extension ${userExtension.extensionLocation.path} in favour of the builtin extension ${extension.extensionLocation.path}.`);
 					return;
 				}
 				// Overwriting a builtin extension inherits the `isBuiltin` property and it doesn't show a warning
